    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257-a1">

                <pb facs="0528" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg508"/>

                <head>Mr. Welles to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Navy Department</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 19, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 14th instant, enclosing a copy of a note addressed to you
                    by Lord Lyons, in which, under the instructions of her Britannic Majesty’s
                    government, he asks to be informed of the grounds upon which the British brigs
                    Volante, of Jersey, and Dashing Wave, of Liverpool, have been captured by United
                    States cruisers at Matamoras.</p>
                <p>In reply, I have to state that the brigs at the time of their capture were in
                    American waters, and, haying contraband cargoes, they were sent in for
                    adjudication. The merchandise of which their cargoes consisted was not believed
                    by the officers of the United States. navy who made the seizure to be either
                    legitimate or neutral. The judgment of the court will be conclusive. </p>
                <p>Very respectfully, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GIDEON WELLES. <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of the
                        Navy.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
